	(footprint "supply1:RotaryEncoder_Alps_EC10E_Horizontal"
		(locked yes)
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "59dc687a-033e-486e-a2d9-c0f209e7ddb6")
		(at 126.5 119 90)
		(descr "Alps EC10E 10 mm hollow-shaft (mouse wheel) encoder, horizontal, through hole. Mounting holes from the Alps EC10E catalog (Update2510, drawings 1-5, same for all heights): 3x d1.0 pins at 2.5 mm pitch, 2x 1.8x2.1 bracket slots 9.0 mm apart (10.8 outer), 2.0 mm behind the pin row. Pins A, B, C left to right in the catalog front view (C = common at the END, not in the middle like EC11). Mirroring between the catalog views is not certain -> CHECK which end pin is C on a sample with an ohmmeter before layout. Shaft axis runs along Y above pin B, at H = 7 / 9 / 11 mm (EC10E1220505 / 0501 / 0503); 1.73 mm hex bore with a 3 deg entry flare. Body outline on F.Fab is approximate.")
